@title The Pinball of the Dead (USA)
@file Pinball of The Dead, The (U).gba
@game APDE
@chip EEPROM (EEPROM_V122; a 4 Kbit chip, dingbat and mgba write 512 bytes)
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@known * checkpoint paused: -- §102: the table's three task creations land 1,302 cycles later in dingbat (EWRAM loads and stores from ROM code under the prefetcher, 3/1 waits, unmeasured on the console), the third after the line-0 IRQ, so the tasks start in another order
@known * checkpoint data_save: -- §102: downstream of the task order set at f2855
@known * checkpoint saved: -- §102: downstream of the task order set at f2855

# Logos and the intro movie, title > GAME START > NORMAL MODE > the first
# table ("Wondering"), its text box tapped away, the ball launched; START
# pauses, SELECT opens DATA SAVE, A + A saves the game into DATA1. [load]:
# CONTINUE > DATA LOAD shows "DATA1 WONDERING (NORMAL)", A + A resumes it.
# Findings (recorded 2026-10-16):
# - In the live session the second reference's intro movie ran on another
#   timeline from f~700 (another scene at f900); replayed by `run` it is a
#   frame from dingbat and mgba (intro_movie_street SLIP -1), so that was the
#   session's doing, not the game's.
# - From the table on dingbat stands alone (its zombies walk on other
#   animation frames and paths; mgba and the second reference share every
#   hash): table_play is a SLIP(+0) only, paused / data_save / saved are
#   MAJOR against both. Mechanism: when the table has loaded (f2855), the
#   main loop calls the task-create routine at 0x08002B20 three times in a
#   row; two of the tasks land in IWRAM slots 0x03001E88 and 0x03001F00
#   (status bytes +0x48 = 0x82 "new", 0x02 once started). Traced from
#   f2852, mgba makes the three calls at V-count 225, 226 and 227, before
#   the V-count IRQ at line 0 (DISPSTAT 0x0029, LYC 0); dingbat makes the
#   first 1,302 cycles later (V-count 226, 227) and the third after that
#   IRQ's handler (0x0300077A -> 0x02002454), at V-count 16. So the task
#   runner's next pass starts a different task (f2856: slot status
#   0x1ED0/0x1F48 = 02/82 in dingbat, 82/02 in both references) and every
#   per-task counter runs a frame apart from there. Before the calls the
#   main thread sits in long BIOS calls (loops at 0x11D0-0x1260) that cost
#   the same per instruction in both (1.58-1.61 cycles a step); where the
#   1.3k cycles come from is not located. The game runs WAITCNT 0x4314
#   (3/1 waits, prefetch on). No console measurement says which side of
#   line 0 the third call falls: an open phase race, not a settled fault.
# - The ball, camera and zombies part from there. The password on DATA
#   SAVE is the same on dingbat and the second reference (3CCC604Z8SS6H
#   in the run), mgba shows another (Q8H8X3ZPZSHGW); the
#   battery files of dingbat and mgba are byte-identical all the same, and
#   every [load] cell resumes the same table.
# - When authored the second reference wrote an 8 KB file and its
#   [load] showed DATA1 EMPTY; APDE is in emu.py's EEPROM_4K since (§94).
[new]
wait 270
checkpoint wow_logo window=30
wait 240
checkpoint intro_movie_date window=30
wait 240
checkpoint intro_movie_street window=30
wait 1170
press START
wait 90
checkpoint main_menu window=30 compare=text
press A
wait 120
checkpoint mode_select window=30 compare=text
press A
wait 120
checkpoint stage_select window=30
press A
wait 245
checkpoint table_intro window=30
tap A times=10 every=30 hold=4
wait 120
checkpoint table_play window=30
press START
wait 60
checkpoint paused window=30
press SELECT
wait 60
checkpoint data_save window=30
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 120
checkpoint saved window=30

[load]
wait 2100
press START
wait 90
press DOWN
wait 30
checkpoint menu_continue window=30 compare=text
press A
wait 90
checkpoint data_load window=30
press A
wait 60
wait 120
press A
wait 240
wait 120
wait 120
checkpoint resumed_table window=30
wait 240
checkpoint resumed_play window=30

